  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 129 AM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nAfter Saturday's front passes, notably drier continental air will \nspread across South Central Texas. While temperatures are not \nexpected to change much in the wake of the front, the decrease in \nmoisture Sunday and potentially Monday will help provide a \ntemporarily drier heat. This is not expected to last for very long \nas subtropical ridge is forecast to re-extend over our area, \nreinstituting southerly flow and allowing higher dew points to \ngradually return. By about midweek, peak afternoon heat indices may \nonce again exceed 105F for the I-35 corridor and low lying plains. \nContinue to practice heat safety and stay cool and hydrated.",
